  "response": "# PR review: petty and single-file findings in `02-react-dashboard`\n\n**Verdict: nothing blocks the merge. 7 findings get a warning and 11 can be ignored.**\n\nThe scan reports 83 findings: 54 medium, 29 low and no high. The highest `agent_risk` anywhere is 0.41. Against an empty baseline, every finding is new in this PR. I used the scan output in the brief and did not run `crimes scan` again.\n\n**Rubric**\n- **Block merge:** severity `high`, or `agent_risk` ≥ 0.50. No finding qualifies.\n- **Warn:** severity `medium`, or `agent_risk` ≥ 0.30.\n- **Ignore:** severity `low` and `agent_risk` < 0.30.\n\n---\n\n## `magic_domain_literal_scatter` (String Sprinkles)\n\n| ID | Location | Sev | agent_risk | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| crime_00001 | `dashboard/final-example/app/lib/actions.ts:43`, literal `\"status\"` | medium (0.50) | **0.41** | **Warn** |\n\nThis has the highest `agent_risk` in the scan. `\"status\"` appears in 5 production files across both dashboard packages. Confidence is 0.85 and `test_gap` is 0.5, so an agent editing one form is likely to miss the others. It doesn't block: severity is medium, `blast_radius` is 0, and the fix is \"small\".\n\n## `duplicated_role_status_plan_check` (repeated status checks)\n\n| ID | Literal | Sev | agent_risk | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| crime_00002 | `\"paid\"`: 4 files, 2 expression shapes | medium (0.55) | **0.36** | **Warn** |\n| crime_00034 | `\"pending\"`: 4 files, 2 expression shapes | medium (0.55) | **0.36** | **Warn** |\n\nThese are the most real \"policy drift\" risk in the PR. The comparisons `invoice.status === \"paid\"` (in `edit-form.tsx`) and `status === \"paid\"` (in `status.tsx`) are spread across 4 files in two packages. A third status added later would have to be wired into every one of them. They are only a warning because confidence is 0.7 and `blast_radius` is 0. These two and crime_00001 are the same underlying problem, and one `invoiceStatus` helper would close all three.\n\n## `commented_out_code` (Commented-Out Corpse)\n\n| ID | Location | Lines | Sev | agent_risk | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| crime_00003 | `starter-example/app/ui/dashboard/latest-invoices.tsx:19-56` | 38 | medium (0.45) | 0.34 | **Warn** |\n| crime_00004 | `starter-example/app/ui/invoices/pagination.tsx:17-50` | 34 | medium (0.45) | 0.34 | **Warn** |\n| crime_00007 | `starter-example/app/ui/dashboard/revenue-chart.tsx:33-62` | 30 | medium (0.45) | 0.31 | **Warn** |\n| crime_00010 | `starter-example/app/query/route.ts:21-25` | 5 | medium (0.45) | 0.30 | **Warn** (borderline) |\n| crime_00037 | `starter-example/app/query/route.ts:5-11` | 7 | low (0.25) | 0.29 | Ignore |\n| crime_00038 | `starter-example/app/ui/dashboard/revenue-chart.tsx:22-24` | 3 | low (0.25) | 0.29 | Ignore |\n| crime_00028 | `final-example/app/lib/data.ts:19-20` | 2 | low (0.25) | 0.28 | Ignore |\n| crime_00029 | `starter-example/app/lib/data.ts:19-20` | 2 | low (0.25) | 0.28 | Ignore |\n| crime_00030 | `final-example/app/query/route.ts:17-20` | 4 | low (0.25) | 0.28 | Ignore |\n| crime_00031 | `starter-example/app/ui/dashboard/cards.tsx:21-28` | 8 | low (0.25) | 0.28 | Ignore |\n\nThe 30–38-line blocks are large enough that an agent could copy them back into live code, which is why they score 0.31–0.34. The 2–8-line ones are mostly `console.log` lines or small stubs.\n\n**Caveat:** all four warnings are in `starter-example/`. That looks like a tutorial scaffold where the commented code is a deliberate \"uncomment this in chapter N\" step. If so, mark them as accepted rather than deleting them. The scores can't tell a scaffold from leftover code.\n\n## Other single-file findings\n\n| Detector | ID | Location | Sev | agent_risk | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `singular_plural_type_mismatch` | crime_00032 | `final-example/app/lib/utils.ts:24` (`revenue: Revenue[]`) | low (0.30) | 0.28 | Ignore |\n| `singular_plural_type_mismatch` | crime_00033 | `starter-example/app/lib/utils.ts:24` | low (0.30) | 0.28 | Ignore |\n| `direct_date` | crime_00048 | `final-example/app/lib/actions.ts:57` (`new Date()`) | low (0.35) | 0.21 | Ignore |\n| `deep_import` | crime_00062 | `seo/components/CodeSampleModal.js` | low (0.35) | 0.07 | Ignore |\n| `deep_import` | crime_00063 | `seo/demo/components/CodeSampleModal.js` | low (0.35) | 0.07 | Ignore |\n\n- **`revenue` naming:** \"revenue\" is a mass noun, so `revenue: Revenue[]` is reasonable naming. Add it to `allowedNames`.\n- **`new Date()`:** the scan's evidence says the clock reading is only recorded, never used to decide a branch.\n- **Deep imports:** the `react-syntax-highlighter` style path is the library's documented import path, and these files sit in the `seo` example, not the dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## Not categorised: outside the petty/single-file scope\n\n- **`exact_duplicate_block` (46 findings, all medium, `agent_risk` 0.28–0.31) and `duplicate_component_shape` (crime_00027, 0.28):** these are cross-package clones. Most come from final-example mirroring starter-example and the `basics/*` step folders copying each other. That's a structural decision about the repo, not a line-level review comment.\n- **`raster_should_be_vector` and `oversized_raster` (18 findings, all low, `agent_risk` 0.04–0.05):** these are assets, not code. The 56–60px customer avatars are photos, so the SVG suggestion doesn't apply.\n\n## Summary\n\n| Verdict | Count | Findings |\n|---|---|---|\n| Block merge | 0 | none (no `high` severity, top `agent_risk` is 0.41) |\n| Warn | 7 | 00001, 00002, 00034, 00003, 00004, 00007, 00010 |\n| Ignore | 11 | 00028–00031, 00037, 00038, 00032, 00033, 00048, 00062, 00063 |\n\n**Recommended follow-up:** extract one invoice-status module with the `paid`/`pending` constants and an `isPaid`/`isPending` helper. That clears the three highest-risk findings. Then decide whether the large commented blocks in starter-example are intentional tutorial stubs or leftovers.",
